<title>USA: Dayton March same store sales rise.</title>
<headline>Dayton March same store sales rise.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dayton Hudson Corp said Thursday its same store sales for March rose 1.9 percent compared with a year ago.</p>
<p>Net retail sales for the five weeks ended April 5 increased 7.8 percent to $2.31 billion from $2.14 billion a year ago.</p>
<p>&quot;March sales were on plan at both Target and Mervyn's, but below expectations at the Department Stores,&quot; Bob Ulrich, chairman and chief executive officer of Dayton Hudson, said in a statement.</p>
</text>
